  "headline": "CBA's APRA Level 2 CET1 ratio rose +10 bpts to 12.3% at 31 Dec 2025 from 12.2% at 31 Dec 2024, broadly flat year-on-year. The movement was driven by capital generated from earnings (cash NPAT up 6% to $5,445m), partly offset by the payment of the 2025 final dividend and higher total RWA ($482.4bn → $505.3bn, +$22.9bn). Higher Credit Risk RWA (+$10.2bn), Operational Risk RWA (+$3.4bn) and Traded Market Risk RWA (+$0.2bn) were partly offset by lower IRRBB RWA (-$4.7bn), which included the impact of adopting the revised APS 117 framework effective 1 October 2025. Other regulatory adjustments and movement in reserves also contributed positively. No separate YoY CET1 bridge chart is published; the bank only provides a half-on-half (Jun 25→Dec 25) walk.",
